LicoUp release source: staged entry for the analytics package's native program.

The analytics package declares a process runtime: one native program that serves
the C11 usage profile (`usage.publish`, `usage.query`, `usage.describe`) to the
client and performs the metrics conversion this package's release declaration
names. The release stage places that compiled program at this path before
`tools/scripts/client-release-package-index.mjs build` packages this directory
into the package payload.

Until it does, this file is the staged entry the committed package declares: the
manifest names a process runtime with no runtimeRef, the release declaration
declares a native executable entry, and the packaging tooling refuses an entry
whose name or first two bytes mark it as a script. Nothing in the repository
executes this file; it exists so the declared native entry is present and the
payload packages deterministically from a checkout.
